      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The main contention is balancing environmental goals against energy security and affordability. Renewable advocates emphasize climate mitigation and sustainable energy transitions, while critics prioritize reliable, domestically controlled energy sources like fossil fuels to ensure independence. Regarding critics' concerns, grid stability issues are real challenges with intermittency, but modern grid technology and energy storage are rapidly advancing to address them. Furthermore, while initial infrastructure costs are high, long-term operational costs of renewables are decreasing, potentially leading to lower overall consumer prices.",
