      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "There is significant merit to the argument that industry groups use cost and reliability concerns as strategic delaying tactics to protect incumbent fossil fuel infrastructure. However, this does not invalidate all concerns; some genuine economic risks related to grid modernization and energy storage integration remain unaddressed. A balanced view suggests that skepticism is multifaceted, stemming from both calculated industry lobbying and legitimate technical hurdles that the transition process must solve.",
      "source": "target",
